FitHub Phase 3 evidence — FR-01 registration consent
Execution date: 2026-10-21 (Europe/Berlin)
Environment: Windows local development; Angular http://localhost:4041; ASP.NET Core http://127.0.0.1:5081; PostgreSQL development database plus Testcontainers PostgreSQL integration suite.
Test account: phase3.acceptance.20261021@fithub.test (synthetic Member; no password recorded in this evidence file).

Expected result
- Consent starts unselected and registration cannot be submitted while it is false.
- Terms of Use and Privacy Notice open real public routes.
- Accepted consent is timestamped and versioned by the backend, not supplied by the browser.

Actual result
- Browser: the registration checkbox started unselected.
- Browser: leaving consent false displayed “You must accept the Terms of Use and acknowledge the Privacy Notice to register” and the form remained on /register without creating an account.
- Browser: /terms and /privacy loaded the academic-demonstration notices.
- API/PostgreSQL: synthetic registration persisted ConsentAcceptedAtUtc and ConsentVersion=1.0. The backend generated both values.
- Automated verification: AuthenticationApiTests covered missing consent, false consent, successful true consent, stored timestamp/version, and unchanged duplicate-email protection.
- Angular verification: registration tests covered requiredTrue, default false, request mapping, and the Terms/Privacy routes.

Decision: PASSED for implementation. The final account-creation click was not repeated through browser automation because account creation requires action-time confirmation; successful registration and database persistence were verified through the API integration workflow.
Build/test corroboration: backend unit 109/109; PostgreSQL integration 85/85; Angular 118/118; production build passed.
Related historical gap: GAP-001. Historical Phase 2 evidence remains unchanged.
